 A condition drawn by several formations is drawn by their joint activity: the first of the laws below says when a part makes the difference to a loss, the others what joint drawing does ([Joint](../../../experiments/integrated-correction/general-framework/generative-basis/lean/becoming/Becoming/Joint.lean), [Continuation](../../../experiments/integrated-correction/general-framework/generative-basis/lean/becoming/Becoming/Continuation.lean), [Exclusion](../../../experiments/integrated-correction/general-framework/generative-basis/lean/becoming/Becoming/Exclusion.lean)).
 
 <a id="r-joint-difference-making"></a>
-**Theorem** (any process; withholding a supplied map on configurations; the move taken held fixed). A part *makes the difference* where the step from a configuration by the move taken breaks a dependence and, the part withheld, the same move can be taken and every step by it keeps the dependence; parts make it *together* where this holds with all of them withheld. Where the step breaks the dependence and, the part withheld, the move can be taken with the dependence holding and met, the part makes the difference exactly where the same move no longer breaks it (`Dependence.makesDifference_iff`). Where the move determines the step and, any single member's part withheld, can be taken with the dependence holding and met, the parts make the difference together while no member alone does exactly where they make it together and withholding any one leaves the same move breaking it (`Dependence.differenceOnlyTogether_iff`); such a difference needs at least two parts. In the witness Pool, with two other drawers the loss is overdetermined: the first drawer's part makes no difference, the first two make it only together, and the [whole-run relational reading](07-SIGNIFICANCE.md#r-relational-reading-comparison) still counts the first drawer as consuming (`Pool.difference_belongs_to_the_joint`). Where withholding leaves the dependence unmet the test is silent; no causal theory or responsibility follows ([record](../results/records/joint-difference-making.md)).
+**Theorem** (any process; withholding a supplied map on configurations; the move taken held fixed). A part *makes the difference* where the step from a configuration by the move taken breaks a dependence and, the part withheld, the same move can be taken and every step by it keeps the dependence; parts make it *together* where this holds with all of them withheld. Where the step breaks the dependence and, the part withheld, the move can be taken with the dependence holding and met, the part makes the difference exactly where the same move no longer breaks it (`Dependence.makesDifference_iff`). Where the move determines the step and, any single member's part withheld, can be taken with the dependence holding and met, the parts make the difference together while no member alone does exactly where they make it together and withholding any one leaves the same move breaking it (`Dependence.differenceOnlyTogether_iff`); such a difference needs at least two parts. In the witness Pool, with two other drawers the loss is overdetermined: the first drawer's part makes no difference, the first two make it only together, and the [whole-run relational reading](07-SIGNIFICANCE.md#r-relational-reading-comparison) still counts the first drawer as consuming (`Pool.difference_only_together`). Where withholding leaves the dependence unmet the test is silent; no causal theory or responsibility follows ([record](../results/records/joint-difference-making.md)).
 
 - **Theorem** (any process; withholding a supplied map on configurations). *Stated at the model.* At a process's model, withholding all parts is passing through their withholdings in turn («历»). Where the move's relation meets the breaking from the configuration and from what each withholding leaves, parts whose but-for statement holds together make the difference only together: it holds for no single one of them (`Becoming.ModelStatements.only_together_reading`, `Becoming.ModelStatements.overdetermined_iff`, `Becoming.ModelStatements.differenceAt`, `Becoming.ModelStatements.withholdAll_iff_li`).
 - **Theorem** (any process; withholding a supplied map on configurations). *Stated at the model.* At the same model, each move's relation fixing its successor, and the move available from what each withholding leaves with the dependence required and met there: the parts make the difference only together exactly where they do together and from what each withholding leaves the move's relation meets the breaking (`Becoming.ModelStatements.differenceOnlyTogether_reading`, `Becoming.ModelStatements.differenceOnlyTogether_iff_model`, `Becoming.ModelStatements.makesDifference_iff`, `Becoming.ModelStatements.makesDifferenceTogether_iff`).
